      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_5791e726df6110d20d5583d56ff1ad8d5c44314cbd0d5d099e2f155c88d145e5",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "The authors propose formal metric similarities connecting their nonlocal Hamiltonian to Hermitian-looking dilation or Berry–Keating operators and explicitly acknowledge that the inverse metric is unbounded. The normalized artifact is a short row-wise interleaving of two columns and ends mid-argument, so operator order, metric factors, state maps, boundary transport, and the claimed direct isospectral calculation cannot be reliably recovered. A domain-preserving bijection and control of the unbounded inverse remain the decisive missing obligations.",
