    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4f3e81a036304f8155f62bf14866a1ad2903649cc627f7d5bd0e31aaecb4d367",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The backward-difference transform turns power solutions of the first-order dilation equation into chosen inverse images −ζ(z,x+1), and the subsequent boundary evaluation ψ_z(0)=0 turns that representation into the condition ζ(z)=0; the continuation's growth and orthogonality discussion then restricts the proposed spectrum to nontrivial-zero states.",
