    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_86362d61fe8a3dbd2cb680ccb42c41e7d6ce96d13d2d4194b128c3be5833990e",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Boundary quantization first supplies states indexed by zeta zeros; a forward-difference adjoint and metric then supply their dual states; substituting the pair into the Mellin-type pairing yields delta-orthogonality when the spectral energies are real, while off-critical zero states are interpreted as self-orthogonal exceptional-point degeneracies with Jordan structure.",
